# Engineering Challenges

The project is designed around real production engineering problems rather than simply building a chatbot.

### Distributed Processing

Document processing is asynchronous and handled by workers.

### Idempotency

Duplicate processing events should not create duplicate versions or indexed content.

### Failure Handling

A document upload can succeed while extraction, embedding, or indexing fails.

The system must represent this accurately instead of incorrectly marking the document as ready.

### Data Consistency

The database might identify v3 as current while the search index still contains v2.

The retrieval layer must prevent stale versions from being returned.

### Permission Security

Authorisation must be enforced during retrieval rather than relying on the LLM to hide restricted information.

### Observability

Important metrics include:

```text
API latency
Document processing latency
Queue depth
Processing failures
Search latency
Retrieval latency
LLM latency
Token usage
Cost per query
Stale retrievals
```

### Auditability

Important knowledge lifecycle events must be traceable.

